### Escenarios de Availability (REST Client / httpyac). Requiere: docker compose up -d availability
### (auth-server 5104, booking-api 5102+, availability 5101) y SERVICEBUS_CONNECTION_STRING en .env para el 202.
### Versión automática de estos escenarios: scripts/live-check.sh

@authUrl = http://localhost:5104
@availabilityUrl = http://localhost:5101
@eventId = 3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6
@userId = 7bb85f64-1111-2222-3333-2c963f66af99
@otherUserId = 9dd07a86-7777-8888-9999-4e185a88c1bb

# ==================================================================
# SUITE HAPPY PATH
# ==================================================================

### H0. Login de usuario (password grant, solo pruebas) → JWT con rol Client
# @name login
POST {{authUrl}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&username=cliente1&password=cliente1-dev

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### H1. Catálogo público (sin token) → 200
GET {{availabilityUrl}}/api/seats

### H2. Reservar B-1 → 202 Accepted + Location (Booking aún no decidió: consistencia eventual)
# @name reserve
POST {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "seatNumber": "B-1", "userId": "{{userId}}", "price": 12000.0 }

###
@reservationId = {{reserve.response.body.reservationId}}

### H3. Estado → 200 (Pending hasta que Booking procese; luego Retained). Repetir hasta Retained
GET {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ==================================================================
# SUITE FALLOS
# ==================================================================

### F1. Sin token → 401
POST {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "seatNumber": "A-1", "userId": "{{userId}}", "price": 15000.0 }

### F2. Rol equivocado (token M2M de servicio, rol Service) → 403
# @name serviceLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=availability&client_secret=availability-secret-dev

###
POST {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{serviceLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "seatNumber": "A-1", "userId": "{{userId}}", "price": 15000.0 }

### F3. userId distinto del sub del token → 403
POST {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "seatNumber": "A-1", "userId": "{{otherUserId}}", "price": 15000.0 }

### F4. Asiento inexistente → 404
POST {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "seatNumber": "Z-9", "userId": "{{userId}}", "price": 15000.0 }

### F5. Asiento no disponible (A-3 sembrado ocupado, o B-1 ya reservado en H2) → 409
POST {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "seatNumber": "A-3", "userId": "{{userId}}", "price": 18000.0 }

### F6. Reserva inexistente (o ajena) → 404
GET {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### F7. Broker no disponible (levantar availability con SERVICEBUS_CONNECTION_STRING vacío) → 503 y el asiento queda libre
POST {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "{{eventId}}", "seatNumber": "A-2", "userId": "{{userId}}", "price": 15000.0 }

### F8. Booking caído (docker compose stop booking-api) → GET de estado 503; no se libera el asiento
GET {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### F9. Auth Server caído (docker compose stop auth-server; reiniciar availability) → GET de estado 503 (el JWT se valida local, falla el token M2M)
GET {{availabilityUrl}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ==================================================================
# LOGIN FEDERADO POR EL IDP EXTERNO (páginas MVC; requiere navegador)
# ==================================================================
# No se puede ejecutar desde este archivo (interviene el navegador y un formulario con form_post). Recorrido manual:
#   1. Abrir http://localhost:5101/Account/Login y pulsar «Ingresar con proveedor externo».
#   2. Availability redirige al Auth Server (/connect/authorize con PKCE S256 e idp_hint=external) y este al IdP (puerto 5105).
#   3. Ingresar con la cuenta del IdP asociada a un usuario del sistema (ana@ejemplo.com); juan@ejemplo.com no está registrado
#      y el Auth Server lo rechaza.
#   4. El IdP devuelve el id_token al Auth Server (nunca a Availability); este vuelve a http://localhost:5101/Account/Callback
#      con un code de un solo uso, que Availability canjea por su cuenta. Se abre la sesión y /Account/Profile muestra el sub.
# Versión automática (curl): scripts/live-check.sh, escenarios E1-E8.
